{
  "metadata": { "name": "Option Pricing", "language_info": { "name": "JavaScipt", "version": "8.0" } },
  "jsnbversion": "v0.1",
  "cells": [
    { "code": "# Voltrix Tests — `/options/price`\n", "status": "", "output": "<h1>Voltrix Tests — <code>/options/price</code></h1>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const BASE = 'http://localhost:8000/v2';\n\nasync function post(path, body) {\n  const res = await fetch(`${BASE}${path}`, {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify(body),\n  });\n  return res.json();\n}", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 1. Black-Scholes — Interactive\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>1. Black-Scholes — Interactive</h2>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Model <select id='op-model'><option value='black_scholes'>black_scholes</option><option value='bachelier'>bachelier</option><option value='monte_carlo'>monte_carlo</option></select></label>\n  <label>Type <select id='op-type'><option value='call'>call</option><option value='put'>put</option></select></label>\n  <label>Spot <input id='op-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='op-strike' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='op-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='op-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='op-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Vol (σ) <input id='op-vol' type='number' value='0.2' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Div Yield <input id='op-div' type='number' value='0.0' step='0.01'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const result = await post('/options/price', {\n  model:           document.getElementById('op-model').value,\n  option_type:     document.getElementById('op-type').value,\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-strike').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-rate').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('op-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('op-expiry').value,\n  dividend_yield:  parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-div').value),\n  volatility:      parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-vol').value),\n  include_insights: true,\n});\nscrib.show('Price: ' + result.price);\nscrib.show('Days to expiry: ' + result.time_to_expiry_days);\nscrib.show(result.volatility_used);\nscrib.show(result.insights);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 2. Put-Call Parity Check\n\nFor the same inputs, call − put should equal S·e^(−qT) − K·e^(−rT). Uses dates entered above.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>2. Put-Call Parity Check</h2>\n<p>For the same inputs, call − put should equal S·e^(−qT) − K·e^(−rT). Uses dates entered above.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const S = parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-spot').value);\nconst K = parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-strike').value);\nconst r = parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-rate').value);\nconst q = parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-div').value);\nconst v = parseFloat(document.getElementById('op-vol').value);\nconst settle = document.getElementById('op-settle').value;\nconst expiry = document.getElementById('op-expiry').value;\nconst T = (new Date(expiry) - new Date(settle)) / (365.25 * 24 * 3600 * 1000);\n\nconst base = { model: 'black_scholes', spot: S, strike: K, rate: r,\n               settlement_date: settle, expiry_date: expiry, dividend_yield: q, volatility: v };\nconst [call, put] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, option_type: 'call' }),\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, option_type: 'put' }),\n]);\nconst parity = S * Math.exp(-q * T) - K * Math.exp(-r * T);\nscrib.show('Call: ' + call.price + ' | Put: ' + put.price);\nscrib.show('Call − Put:         ' + (call.price - put.price).toFixed(6));\nscrib.show('S·e⁻ᵠᵀ − K·e⁻ʳᵀ:  ' + parity.toFixed(6));\nscrib.show('Parity holds: ' + (Math.abs((call.price - put.price) - parity) < 0.001));", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 3. Vol Surface — Matrix Interpolation\n\nQuery a 3×2 vol matrix at a chosen strike and expiry.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>3. Vol Surface — Matrix Interpolation</h2>\n<p>Query a 3×2 vol matrix at a chosen strike and expiry.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Query Strike <input id='surf-strike' type='number' value='105'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='surf-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='surf-expiry' type='date' value='2026-10-01'></label>\n  <label>Spot <input id='surf-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='surf-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const result = await post('/options/price', {\n  model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call',\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('surf-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('surf-strike').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('surf-rate').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('surf-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('surf-expiry').value,\n  volatility: {\n    vol_type: 'log_normal', surface_type: 'matrix',\n    data: {\n      strikes: [90, 100, 110], maturities: [0.5, 1.0],\n      vol_matrix: [[0.25, 0.24], [0.20, 0.19], [0.22, 0.21]],\n    },\n    interpolation: 'bilinear', extrapolation: 'flat',\n  },\n  include_insights: true,\n});\nscrib.show('Price: ' + result.price);\nscrib.show('Days to expiry: ' + result.time_to_expiry_days);\nscrib.show('Interpolated σ: ' + result.volatility_used.value + ' (source: ' + result.volatility_used.source + ')');\nscrib.show(result.insights);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 4. Monte Carlo — Path Count Comparison\n\nCompare MC price accuracy as number of simulations increases.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>4. Monte Carlo — Path Count Comparison</h2>\n<p>Compare MC price accuracy as number of simulations increases.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Spot <input id='mc-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='mc-strike' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Vol <input id='mc-vol' type='number' value='0.2' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='mc-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='mc-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Seed <input id='mc-seed' type='number' value='42'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const S    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('mc-spot').value);\nconst K    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('mc-strike').value);\nconst v    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('mc-vol').value);\nconst settle = document.getElementById('mc-settle').value;\nconst expiry = document.getElementById('mc-expiry').value;\nconst seed = parseInt(document.getElementById('mc-seed').value);\n\nconst base = { option_type: 'call', spot: S, strike: K, rate: 0.05,\n               settlement_date: settle, expiry_date: expiry, volatility: v };\nconst [bs, mc1k, mc10k, mc50k] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, model: 'black_scholes' }),\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, model: 'monte_carlo', num_simulations: 1000,  seed }),\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, model: 'monte_carlo', num_simulations: 10000, seed }),\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, model: 'monte_carlo', num_simulations: 50000, seed }),\n]);\nscrib.show('BS (exact):       ' + bs.price);\nscrib.show('MC  1,000 paths:  ' + mc1k.price  + ' | error: ' + Math.abs(mc1k.price  - bs.price).toFixed(5));\nscrib.show('MC 10,000 paths:  ' + mc10k.price + ' | error: ' + Math.abs(mc10k.price - bs.price).toFixed(5));\nscrib.show('MC 50,000 paths:  ' + mc50k.price + ' | error: ' + Math.abs(mc50k.price - bs.price).toFixed(5));", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 5. CEV Model — Beta Sweep\n\nSee how price changes as β moves from 0.1 (near-normal) to 1.0 (log-normal).\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>5. CEV Model — Beta Sweep</h2>\n<p>See how price changes as β moves from 0.1 (near-normal) to 1.0 (log-normal).</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Spot <input id='cev-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='cev-strike' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>σ <input id='cev-vol' type='number' value='0.2' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Paths <input id='cev-sims' type='number' value='20000'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const S    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('cev-spot').value);\nconst K    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('cev-strike').value);\nconst sig  = parseFloat(document.getElementById('cev-vol').value);\nconst sims = parseInt(document.getElementById('cev-sims').value);\n\nconst betas = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0];\nconst results = await Promise.all(betas.map(b =>\n  post('/options/price', {\n    model: 'cev', option_type: 'call', spot: S, strike: K, rate: 0.05,\n    settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n    volatility: { surface_type: 'constant', data: { vol: sig }, other_params: { cev_beta: b } },\n    num_simulations: sims, seed: 42,\n  })\n));\nscrib.show('β     | Price');\nbetas.forEach((b, i) => scrib.show('β=' + b.toFixed(1) + '  | ' + results[i].price.toFixed(5)));", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 6. SABR — Interactive Pricing\n\nHagan et al. (2002) SABR formula resolves an implied BS vol at (K, T, F) and prices via Black-Scholes.\n`α` sets the overall vol level, `β` the backbone (0=normal, 1=log-normal),\n`ρ` the skew (negative → downside), `ν` the smile curvature.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>6. SABR — Interactive Pricing</h2>\n<p>SABR resolves an implied BS vol at (K, T) via Hagan formula, then prices with Black-Scholes.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Type <select id='sabr-type'><option value='call'>call</option><option value='put'>put</option></select></label>\n  <label>Spot <input id='sabr-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='sabr-strike' type='number' value='105'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='sabr-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='sabr-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='sabr-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>α (alpha) <input id='sabr-alpha' type='number' value='0.3' step='0.05'></label>\n  <label>β (beta) <input id='sabr-beta' type='number' value='0.5' step='0.1' min='0' max='1'></label>\n  <label>ρ (rho) <input id='sabr-rho' type='number' value='-0.3' step='0.1' min='-0.99' max='0.99'></label>\n  <label>ν (nu) <input id='sabr-nu' type='number' value='0.4' step='0.05'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const result = await post('/options/price', {\n  model:           'black_scholes',\n  option_type:     document.getElementById('sabr-type').value,\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-strike').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-rate').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('sabr-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('sabr-expiry').value,\n  volatility: {\n    surface_type: 'sabr',\n    other_params: {\n      alpha: parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-alpha').value),\n      beta:  parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-beta').value),\n      rho:   parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-rho').value),\n      nu:    parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-nu').value),\n    },\n  },\n});\nscrib.show('Price: ' + result.price);\nscrib.show('SABR implied σ: ' + result.volatility_used.value + ' (source: ' + result.volatility_used.source + ')');", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 7. SABR — Smile Sweep (IV vs Strike)\n\nFixed SABR parameters, sweep strikes 80–120. Negative ρ produces downside skew\n(lower-strike options have higher implied vol).\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>7. SABR — Smile Sweep</h2>\n<p>Fixed SABR params, implied vol across strikes 80–120. Negative ρ → downside skew.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Spot <input id='sabr-sw-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='sabr-sw-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='sabr-sw-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='sabr-sw-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>α <input id='sabr-sw-alpha' type='number' value='0.3' step='0.05'></label>\n  <label>β <input id='sabr-sw-beta' type='number' value='0.5' step='0.1'></label>\n  <label>ρ <input id='sabr-sw-rho' type='number' value='-0.3' step='0.1'></label>\n  <label>ν <input id='sabr-sw-nu' type='number' value='0.4' step='0.05'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const S      = parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-sw-spot').value);\nconst r      = parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-sw-rate').value);\nconst settle = document.getElementById('sabr-sw-settle').value;\nconst expiry = document.getElementById('sabr-sw-expiry').value;\nconst sabrP  = {\n  alpha: parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-sw-alpha').value),\n  beta:  parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-sw-beta').value),\n  rho:   parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-sw-rho').value),\n  nu:    parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-sw-nu').value),\n};\n\nconst strikes = [80, 85, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 115, 120];\nconst results = await Promise.all(strikes.map(K =>\n  post('/options/price', {\n    model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call',\n    spot: S, strike: K, rate: r,\n    settlement_date: settle, expiry_date: expiry,\n    volatility: { surface_type: 'sabr', other_params: sabrP },\n  })\n));\nscrib.show('Strike | SABR σ   | Call Price');\nstrikes.forEach((K, i) =>\n  scrib.show('  ' + String(K).padStart(3) + '  | ' +\n    results[i].volatility_used.value.toFixed(5) + ' | ' +\n    results[i].price.toFixed(5))\n);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 8. SVI — Interactive Pricing\n\nGatheral raw SVI parametrisation. Total implied variance:\n`w(k) = a + b·(ρ·(k−m) + √((k−m)² + σ²))` where `k = ln(K/F)`.\nImplied vol = √(w/T).\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>8. SVI — Interactive Pricing</h2>\n<p>Gatheral raw SVI. w(k) = a + b·(ρ·(k−m) + √((k−m)²+σ²)), implied vol = √(w/T).</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Type <select id='svi-type'><option value='call'>call</option><option value='put'>put</option></select></label>\n  <label>Spot <input id='svi-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='svi-strike' type='number' value='105'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='svi-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='svi-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='svi-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>a <input id='svi-a' type='number' value='0.04' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>b <input id='svi-b' type='number' value='0.2' step='0.05'></label>\n  <label>ρ (rho) <input id='svi-rho' type='number' value='-0.3' step='0.1'></label>\n  <label>m <input id='svi-m' type='number' value='0.0' step='0.05'></label>\n  <label>σ (sigma) <input id='svi-sigma' type='number' value='0.3' step='0.05'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const result = await post('/options/price', {\n  model:           'black_scholes',\n  option_type:     document.getElementById('svi-type').value,\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('svi-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('svi-strike').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('svi-rate').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('svi-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('svi-expiry').value,\n  volatility: {\n    surface_type: 'svi',\n    other_params: {\n      a:     parseFloat(document.getElementById('svi-a').value),\n      b:     parseFloat(document.getElementById('svi-b').value),\n      rho:   parseFloat(document.getElementById('svi-rho').value),\n      m:     parseFloat(document.getElementById('svi-m').value),\n      sigma: parseFloat(document.getElementById('svi-sigma').value),\n    },\n  },\n});\nscrib.show('Price: ' + result.price);\nscrib.show('SVI implied σ: ' + result.volatility_used.value + ' (source: ' + result.volatility_used.source + ')');", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 9. SVI — Smile Sweep (IV vs Strike)\n\nSVI naturally produces a smile centred around m (the log-moneyness shift).\nNegative ρ adds skew, making lower strikes relatively more expensive.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>9. SVI — Smile Sweep</h2>\n<p>SVI smile shape across strikes 80–120. ρ controls asymmetry.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const sviP  = { a: 0.04, b: 0.2, rho: -0.3, m: 0.0, sigma: 0.3 };\nconst strikes = [80, 85, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 115, 120];\nconst results = await Promise.all(strikes.map(K =>\n  post('/options/price', {\n    model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call',\n    spot: 100, strike: K, rate: 0.05,\n    settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n    volatility: { surface_type: 'svi', other_params: sviP },\n  })\n));\nscrib.show('Strike | SVI σ    | Call Price');\nstrikes.forEach((K, i) =>\n  scrib.show('  ' + String(K).padStart(3) + '  | ' +\n    results[i].volatility_used.value.toFixed(5) + ' | ' +\n    results[i].price.toFixed(5))\n);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 10. Heston — Semi-Analytic Pricing\n\nHeston (1993) stochastic-vol model with semi-analytic characteristic-function pricing.\n`v0` = initial variance (vol ≈ √v0), `kappa` = mean-reversion speed, `theta` = long-run variance,\n`sigma_v` = vol of vol, `rho` = spot-variance correlation (negative → left skew).\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>10. Heston — Semi-Analytic Pricing</h2>\n<p>Heston (1993) characteristic-function pricer. v0 = initial variance (vol ≈ √v0), θ = long-run variance.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Type <select id='hest-type'><option value='call'>call</option><option value='put'>put</option></select></label>\n  <label>Spot <input id='hest-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='hest-strike' type='number' value='105'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='hest-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='hest-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='hest-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>v0 (init var) <input id='hest-v0' type='number' value='0.04' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>κ (kappa) <input id='hest-kappa' type='number' value='2.0' step='0.5'></label>\n  <label>θ (theta) <input id='hest-theta' type='number' value='0.04' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>σᵥ (sigma_v) <input id='hest-sv' type='number' value='0.3' step='0.05'></label>\n  <label>ρ (rho) <input id='hest-rho' type='number' value='-0.7' step='0.1'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const hp = {\n  v0:      parseFloat(document.getElementById('hest-v0').value),\n  kappa:   parseFloat(document.getElementById('hest-kappa').value),\n  theta:   parseFloat(document.getElementById('hest-theta').value),\n  sigma_v: parseFloat(document.getElementById('hest-sv').value),\n  rho:     parseFloat(document.getElementById('hest-rho').value),\n};\nconst result = await post('/options/price', {\n  model:           'heston',\n  option_type:     document.getElementById('hest-type').value,\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('hest-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('hest-strike').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('hest-rate').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('hest-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('hest-expiry').value,\n  volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: hp },\n});\nscrib.show('Price (semi-analytic): ' + result.price);\nscrib.show('Reference σ₀ = √v0:   ' + result.volatility_used.value);\nscrib.show('Model: ' + result.model_used + ' | Days: ' + result.time_to_expiry_days);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 11. Heston — Semi-Analytic vs Monte Carlo Cross-Check\n\nBoth methods should agree within a few basis points. MC variance falls with more paths.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>11. Heston — Semi-Analytic vs Monte Carlo Cross-Check</h2>\n<p>The two pricing paths should agree within a few cents for sufficient path counts.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Spot <input id='hmc-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='hmc-strike' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Paths <input id='hmc-sims' type='number' value='50000'></label>\n  <label>Seed <input id='hmc-seed' type='number' value='42'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const S    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('hmc-spot').value);\nconst K    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('hmc-strike').value);\nconst sims = parseInt(document.getElementById('hmc-sims').value);\nconst seed = parseInt(document.getElementById('hmc-seed').value);\nconst hp   = { v0: 0.04, kappa: 2.0, theta: 0.04, sigma_v: 0.3, rho: -0.7 };\nconst base = {\n  model: 'heston', option_type: 'call',\n  spot: S, strike: K, rate: 0.05,\n  settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n};\n\nconst [analytic, mc] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: { ...hp } } }),\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, num_simulations: sims, seed,\n    volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: { ...hp, use_mc: true } } }),\n]);\nscrib.show('Semi-analytic:  ' + analytic.price);\nscrib.show('Monte Carlo:    ' + mc.price + '  (' + sims.toLocaleString() + ' paths, seed=' + seed + ')');\nscrib.show('Difference:     ' + Math.abs(analytic.price - mc.price).toFixed(5));", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 12. Heston — Put-Call Parity\n\nPut-call parity must hold: call − put = S·e^(−qT) − K·e^(−rT).\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>12. Heston — Put-Call Parity</h2>\n<p>call − put = S·e⁻ᵠᵀ − K·e⁻ʳᵀ must hold for Heston.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const S = 100, K = 100, r = 0.05, q = 0.0, T = 1.0;\nconst hp = { v0: 0.04, kappa: 2.0, theta: 0.04, sigma_v: 0.3, rho: -0.7 };\nconst base = {\n  model: 'heston', spot: S, strike: K, rate: r, dividend_yield: q,\n  settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n  volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: hp },\n};\nconst [call, put] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, option_type: 'call' }),\n  post('/options/price', { ...base, option_type: 'put' }),\n]);\nconst parity = S * Math.exp(-q * T) - K * Math.exp(-r * T);\nscrib.show('Heston call:       ' + call.price);\nscrib.show('Heston put:        ' + put.price);\nscrib.show('Call − Put:        ' + (call.price - put.price).toFixed(6));\nscrib.show('S·e⁻ᵠᵀ − K·e⁻ʳᵀ: ' + parity.toFixed(6));\nscrib.show('Parity error:      ' + Math.abs((call.price - put.price) - parity).toFixed(8));", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 13. Heston — Strike Sweep\n\nSweep strikes 80–120. Negative ρ suppresses OTM call prices (left skew).\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>13. Heston — Strike Sweep</h2>\n<p>Negative ρ → OTM calls cheaper, OTM puts more expensive (left skew).</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const hp      = { v0: 0.04, kappa: 2.0, theta: 0.04, sigma_v: 0.3, rho: -0.7 };\nconst strikes = [80, 85, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 115, 120];\nconst results = await Promise.all(strikes.map(K =>\n  post('/options/price', {\n    model: 'heston', option_type: 'call',\n    spot: 100, strike: K, rate: 0.05,\n    settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n    volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: hp },\n  })\n));\nscrib.show('Strike | Heston Price | Ref σ₀');\nstrikes.forEach((K, i) =>\n  scrib.show('  ' + String(K).padStart(3) + '  | ' +\n    results[i].price.toFixed(5).padStart(11) + '  | ' +\n    results[i].volatility_used.value.toFixed(4))\n);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 14. Error Handling\n\n- Negative spot → 422 validation error.\n- Heston `surface_type` with missing required params → 422 validation error.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>14. Error Handling</h2>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const err1 = await post('/options/price', {\n  model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call',\n  spot: -50, strike: 100, rate: 0.05,\n  settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n  volatility: 0.2,\n});\nscrib.show('Negative spot → ' + JSON.stringify(err1).slice(0, 120));\n\nconst err2 = await post('/options/price', {\n  model: 'heston', option_type: 'call',\n  spot: 100, strike: 100, rate: 0.05,\n  settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n  volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: { v0: 0.04 } },\n});\nscrib.show('Missing Heston params → ' + JSON.stringify(err2).slice(0, 180));", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" }
  ],
  "source": "https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/scribbler",
  "run_on_load": false
}
